Build UserIds/UserNames arrays
       ↓
Get signatures
       ↓
Base64
       ↓
Copy template to unique XLSX
       ↓
Run Office Script
       ↓
Completed XLSX in SharePoint
       ↓
PDF Converter
       ↓
PDF
       ↓
Save PDF to SharePoint
       ↓
Email PDF

Which PDF converter?

There are three practical choices:

1. Muhimbi PDF — good fit for Power Automate and specifically has a Convert Excel document action.


2. Encodian — also designed for Power Automate document conversion.


3. Adobe PDF Services — another option if your organization already has Adobe licensing.



Muhimbi's connector specifically exposes Convert Excel document, accepting the Excel filename and file content and producing PDF or other formats.  Encodian also provides Power Automate PDF conversion capabilities, but requires an Encodian subscription/API connection.  Adobe PDF Services provides file-content-based PDF conversion as well. 

For your current setup, I would use Muhimbi if your company permits it.


