One important correction to my previous recommendation

You do not need OneDrive at all for the Excel portion.

The Excel Online (Business) connector supports files stored in SharePoint, including using a SharePoint file identifier as the workbook. 

So your generated workbook can remain entirely here:

GNS Reactivation Archive
└── Generated Excel
    ├── User Account Reactivation-125-20261006-093500.xlsx
    ├── User Account Reactivation-126-20261006-093502.xlsx
    └── User Account Reactivation-127-20261006-093504.xlsx

Only the PDF conversion requires a separate service.

My recommendation

For your company environment, I'd choose:

SharePoint + Excel Online (Business) + Office Scripts + Muhimbi + Outlook

rather than trying to make OneDrive available just for this flow.

That gives you:

✅ No OneDrive dependency

✅ Excel remains in SharePoint

✅ Unique Excel per request

✅ Office Script signatures

✅ PDF conversion

✅ PDF SharePoint archive

✅ Email attachment

✅ Multiple requests can generate separate files

✅ Easier auditing


If Muhimbi is also unavailable/blocked in your organization, then the next best option is Encodian or Adobe PDF Services; both have current Power Automate connectors capable of document/PDF conversion. 


